# Git for Windows has core.autocrlf=true system-wide on the machine this
# project is developed on, so a checkout here rewrites text files to CRLF. For
# most of the repo that is harmless. For the files Linux tooling reads it is
# not: a shell script whose shebang line ends in CR fails with "bad
# interpreter", and a Dockerfile's line continuations are fragile the same way.
#
# These therefore keep LF in every checkout, on every platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker/Caddyfile text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
